.TH WRAITH 1 "October 2026" "wraith 1.5.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wraith \- Kernel-grade network anonymization and session cleanups framework
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wraith
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wraith
is an enterprise-grade Linux network privacy and traffic anonymization framework. It enforces transparent Tor routing,
kernel-level Netfilter isolation, RFC 1035 wire-format DNS sinkholing, and cross-layer L4/L7 OS fingerprint normalization.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBstart\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Initiates the kernel network privacy session, configures Netfilter tables, starts the local DNSSEC resolver, and bootstraps Tor routing.
.TP
\fBstop\fR [\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-forensic\-self\-destruct\fR]
Gracefully terminates the active session, flushes TransPort redirects, restores original nameservers, and unlocks /etc/resolv.conf.
.TP
\fBstatus\fR, \fBinfo\fR
Displays live network interfaces, active Tor circuits, IP leak diagnostics, and firewall state.
.TP
\fBexec\fR \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS...\fR]
Executes an application inside the active Wraith network namespace as the invoking user.
.TP
\fBswitch\fR
Requests a new Tor circuit and rotates the exit node identity.
.TP
\fBtest\fR
Runs the comprehensive leak verification suite (IPv4, IPv6, DNSSEC, WebRTC).
.TP
\fBdoctor\fR
Executes an audit on kernel capabilities, netfilter modules, Tor binaries, and system utilities.
.TP
\fBbenchmark\fR
Runs high-performance cryptographic cipher and kernel subsystem throughput benchmarks.
.TP
\fBcleanup\fR [\fB\-\-full\fR]
Performs session cleanup system sanitization, wiping RAM caches, system logs, and swap space.
.TP
\fBshred\fR \fIFILE\fR [\fB\-p\fR \fIPASSES\fR]
Securely overwrites and deletes a file using DoD 5220.22-M multi-pass sanitization standard (default: 7 passes).
.TP
\fBfetch\fR \fIURL\fR \fB\-o\fR \fIOUTPUT\fR [\fB\-\-tls\-profile\fR \fIPROFILE\fR]
Retrieves HTTPS content over Tor using authentic browser-profile TLS (Chrome, Firefox, Safari) and HTTP/2 handshakes.
.TP
\fBinterfaces\fR [\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-all\fR]
Enumerates host network interfaces and physical/virtual adapter attributes.
.TP
\fBmac\fR
Randomizes network interface L2 MAC address using kernel CSPRNG and sets a randomized benign hostname.
.TP
\fBprofile\fR \fINAME\fR
Applies a geographic Tor exit node profile: stealth, speed, journalists, research, or darkweb.
.TP
\fBupdate\fR
Fast-forwards the source repository from the official GitHub upstream.
.TP
\fBmonitor\fR
Launches the packet telemetry monitor.
.TP
\fBconfig\fR [\fBshow\fR|\fBget\fR|\fBset\fR]
Manages persistent configuration settings in /etc/wraith/config.toml.
.TP
\fBbridge\fR [\fBmoat\fR|\fBlist\fR]
Manages censorship circumvention bridges or queries Tor BridgeDB via the Moat Protocol (JSON-API).
.TP
\fBdoh\fR [\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-select\fR]
Inspects or selects DNS-over-HTTPS (DoH) upstream resolvers via interactive TUI menu.
.TP
\fBnetwork\fR \fBreset\fR [\fITARGET\fR]
Network operations and emergency recovery interface. Recovers the recorded session and restores saved settings.
.TP
\fBreset\fR [\fITARGET\fR]
Recover the complete recorded Wraith session using the same ownership-checked path as stop. All targets, including dns and firewall, restore the complete session. Missing state changes nothing; failed cleanup returns an error and retains recovery records.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-start\fR
Quick start shortcut applying specified or default anonymization options.
.TP
\fB\-x\fR, \fB\-\-stop\fR
Quick stop shortcut restoring original network settings.
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-info\fR, \fB\-\-status\fR
Display telemetry dashboard and active circuits.
.TP
\fB\-F\fR, \fB\-\-full\-security\fR
Strict security preset. Enforces Tor transparent proxying, DNSSEC validation, matching L4/TLS profiles, CSPRNG MAC rotation, and memory lockdown.
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-namespace\fR
Restricts routing to an isolated Linux Network Namespace (10.200.1.0/24) via virtual ethernet pair.
.TP
\fB\-I\fR, \fB\-\-interface\fR \fIINTERFACE\fR
Target network interface adapter for L2/L3 operations (e.g. eth0, wlan0).
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-mac\fR
Randomizes network interface L2 MAC address using kernel CSPRNG and sets a benign hostname.
.TP
\fB\-D\fR, \fB\-\-doh\fR \fIPRESET_OR_URL\fR
Configures upstream DNS-over-HTTPS resolver preset (quad9, mullvad, cloudflare, adguard, controld, google) or custom URL.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-profile\fR \fIPROFILE\fR
Enforces geographic Tor exit node profile (stealth, speed, journalists, research, darkweb).
.TP
\fB\-\-morph\-l4\fR \fIPROFILE\fR
Layer 4 TCP normalization profile: auto (follows TLS profile), windows, windows11, macos, linux, or off.
.TP
\fB\-\-tls\-profile\fR \fIBROWSER\fR
Browser TLS impersonation profile for session DoH and cover traffic: chrome, firefox, or safari.
.TP
\fB\-W\fR, \fB\-\-wireguard\fR \fICONFIG\fR
Encapsulates Tor traffic inside a kernel WireGuard tunnel for multi-hop transport privacy and censorship resistance.
.TP
\fB\-b\fR, \fB\-\-bridge\fR
Routes traffic through censorship-resistant Tor bridges.
.TP
\fB\-\-bridge\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR
Pluggable transport mechanism: obfs4, snowflake, meek, or moat.
.TP
\fB\-\-onion\fR \fIVIRT_PORT:TARGET_PORT\fR
Arms an ephemeral v3 Onion Hidden Service forwarding virtual port to target port.
.TP
\fB\-\-jitter\fR, \fB\-\-jitter\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR
Sends bounded, randomized HTTPS cover requests through Tor to the specified endpoint.
.TP
\fB\-\-rotate\-interval\fR \fISECONDS\fR
Automatically rotates the Tor exit node identity every N seconds.
.TP
\fB\-\-shaper\fR
Applies Linux TC/Netem latency distribution, jitter, and loss settings.
.TP
\fB\-\-browser\-shield\fR
Injects anti-fingerprinting canvas, audio, font, and WebGL protection profiles into supported browsers.
.TP
\fB\-\-font\-sandbox\fR
Restricts OS-level font discovery via a localized Fontconfig sandbox.
.TP
\fB\-\-display\-sandbox\fR
Spawns an isolated X11 virtual display sandbox (Xvfb 1920x1080@24bit) to mask physical display EDID.
.TP
\fB\-\-honey\-ports\fR
Arms localhost deception honey-port traps on common lateral movement ports (2222, 3306, 5432, 6379, 8080, 27017).
.TP
\fB\-\-honey\-lan\fR
Binds honeypot traps to the selected private LAN interface address.
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-mask\fR
Normalizes namespace TCP and Tor access-link initial SYNs.
.TP
\fB\-\-machine\-id\fR
Rotates unique OS /etc/machine-id and system hardware identifiers.
.TP
\fB\-K\fR, \fB\-\-aggressive\-masquerade\fR
Sets the process communication label to [kworker/u16:0]; the executable path is unchanged.
.TP
\fB\-A\fR, \fB\-\-aggressive\-anti\-debug\fR
Enforces an aggressive anti-debugging probe; immediately triggers SIGKILL if attached to a debugger.
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-forensic\-wipe\-logs\fR
Irreversibly eradicates system authentication logs, event logs, and user shell history files upon exit.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-forensic\-self\-destruct\fR
Cryptographically shreds the binary from disk and wipes memory artifacts upon session shutdown.
.TP
\fB\-M\fR, \fB\-\-monitor\fR
Launches the real-time packet telemetry monitor.
.TP
\fB\-R\fR, \fB\-N\fR, \fB\-\-reset\fR
Recovery shortcut for the complete recorded Wraith session. Preserves unrelated resources and reports incomplete cleanup.
.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-update\fR
Fast-forwards source repository from official GitHub upstream.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose debug tracing output.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help message and exit.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WRAITH_LANG
Overrides system locale and sets the interface language (e.g. "en", "tr", "de", "fr", "es", "ru", "zh").
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/run/wraith.state
Runtime session state and rollback snapshot (symlinked to /run/wraith.state on modern distributions).
.TP
.I /etc/wraith/config.toml
Main configuration file.
.TP
.I /etc/tor/wraithrc
Dedicated Tor daemon configuration generated for the active session.
.TP
.I /var/lib/wraith/
Persistent directory for Tor daemon state, consensus cache, and cryptographic keys.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
General operational error or verification failure.
.TP
.B 2
Insufficient permissions (root privileges required).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tor (1),
.BR iptables (8),
.BR ip-netns (8)
